    "categoryConfidence": "medium",
    "campaign": "International Coffee Day",
    "caption": "The great thing about coffee is that not only is it an essential everyday beverage, but it also makes for a delicious dessert ingredient.\n\nTake this Cappuccino Mousse Trifle for example, made with Nescafé Gold Blend Medium Roast. A typical trifle comes dressed in chocolate and strawberries, but for this dessert, we gave it a bit of a tiramisu spin by using coffee and biscuits instead. Add a splash of dark rum to booze up this layered dessert, if you wish! Grab your eco-friendly shopping bag and grab all the ingredients that you need for this recipe at #TheMarketplace!\n\nServing Time: 1 hour\nYield: 2-4 servings\n\nIngredients\n\nFor the coffee mousse:\n2 ½ tsps. unflavored gelatin powder \n3 tbsps. cold water\n3 large egg yolks\n⅔ cup brown sugar\n2 cups whole milk\n2 tbsps. Nescafé Gold Blend Medium Roast\n1 ½ cups heavy cream, cold\n\nFor assembly:\n1 cup whipped cream\n1 cup lightly crushed biscuits or cookies\nDark chocolate shavings to garnish\n\nProcedure\n1. Bloom gelatin in cold water for 5 mins. Set aside. In a bowl, whisk egg yolks and brown sugar.\n2. Stir milk with Nescafé Gold Blend Medium Roast in a saucepan over low heat. Simmer then slowly whisk half into the yolk mixture. Return everything to the pan, whisking until thickened. Once bubbling, transfer to a bowl and mix in gelatin. Cover and cool to room temperature.\n3. Beat cold heavy cream until stiff. Mix ⅓ into the coffee custard and gently fold in the rest.\n4. In the serving glasses, layer crushed biscuits, whipped cream, and the coffee mousse. Repeat layers and top with dark chocolate shavings.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/ShopNowGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
